1
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:26,040
In academic texts, we also make point lineups.

2
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:29,180
It may be for slightly different reasons

3
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:32,512
but above all if you want to do things clear-

4
00:00:32,768 --> 00:00:35,262
or when you want to highlight specific things-

5
00:00:35,262 --> 00:00:37,120
Or when you want to clarify things.

6
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:40,080
But when should you make setups

7
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:44,040
And not reproduce the information in your body text?

8
00:00:44,288 --> 00:00:47,862
There are some guidelines to follow.

9
00:00:47,862 --> 00:00:49,408
They look like this:

10
00:00:50,176 --> 00:00:54,272
When you want to emphasize some information.

11
00:00:54,528 --> 00:00:57,600
When a sentence contains long enumerations.

12
00:00:57,856 --> 00:01:01,952
When you want to explain or sort out complicated facts.

13
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:06,816
All this is about facilitating reading.

14
00:01:07,584 --> 00:01:13,728
If you need to make a point lineup, there are guidelines to follow.

15
00:01:14,496 --> 00:01:19,360
You have to be careful about how to construct your joints in your set up.

16
00:01:19,616 --> 00:01:24,224
You should construct them similarly in both form and content.

17
00:01:24,992 --> 00:01:29,088
You can formulate your points in slightly different ways.

18
00:01:29,344 --> 00:01:34,208
For example, your joints may be focused on words or phrase

19
00:01:35,232 --> 00:01:36,512
on a sent-

20
00:01:36,768 --> 00:01:38,560
or one or more sentences.

21
00:01:42,912 --> 00:01:43,680
But...

22
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:47,540
You must be careful not to mix the way you write your joints.

23
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:49,700
Namely

24
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:53,260
You must not mix individual words with complete sentences.

25
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:54,680
You choose a way

26
00:01:54,944 --> 00:01:58,016
to formulate yourself in your set -up.

27
00:01:58,784 --> 00:02:02,368
If you are going to make a point lineup with short joints

28
00:02:02,624 --> 00:02:05,184
Has each joint lowercase.

29
00:02:05,696 --> 00:02:06,976
It may look like this.

30
00:02:07,232 --> 00:02:09,792
"In the first place you can seek answers by"

31
00:02:10,304 --> 00:02:14,656
"Read your course literature, visit your nearest library, talk to a student friend."

32
00:03:13,956 --> 00:03:14,816
Then it will be with a colon.

33
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:17,220
But is it not an independent batch

34
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:18,840
it will not be the colon.

35
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:24,600
It depends on how you have built up your meaning structure.

36
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:28,640
Your joints can be marked in slightly different ways.

37
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:37,520
You can use point, tank line, letters (common) or numbers.

38
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:41,340
When you write with numbers it may look like this.

39
00:03:41,340 --> 00:03:43,560
You have 1.2 and 3 and always a point after.

40
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:46,560
Letters have a final bracket behind it.

41
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:51,920
Would you like to refer to your point lineup further in your body text

42
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:57,580
Then 1, 2 and 3, or A, B and C are best to use.

43
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:00,400
It is not possible to refer back to point or tank line.

44
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:03,580
Would you like to comment on your points

45
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:06,900
Do you use any of these.

46
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:09,600
You can also use both of these.

47
00:04:09,856 --> 00:04:12,928
For example, if you have a first joint with numbers

48
00:04:13,184 --> 00:04:15,488
and wants to during e.g.
the third-

49
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:32,840
You can refer to both numbers or letters further in your text

50
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:35,980
If you want to comment on what is in the point lineup.

51
00:04:38,015 --> 00:04:38,783
So...

52
00:04:39,295 --> 00:04:41,855
Consider when using point set up.

53
00:04:42,623 --> 00:04:45,183
Make sure you are constructing similarly.

54
00:04:45,951 --> 00:04:48,767
Formalia and punctuation you must follow

55
00:04:49,023 --> 00:04:50,559
So as I went through in this movie.

56
00:04:51,327 --> 00:04:56,447
Make sure to use point set up to increase readability in your text.

57
00:04:57,727 --> 00:04:59,775
So have you made point lineups

58
00:05:00,031 --> 00:05:02,335
Look how they look.

59
00:05:02,591 --> 00:05:05,151
Fix what may need to be addressed.
